Christopher did not speak for several minutes. He was not certain how he felt. Although perhaps it was too early to say with absolute certainty, it seemed that he would not be a father—not right away, at least. Father . . . to become a father. Dear God, it was true: sooner or later it would happen. Sooner or later Anna would ask to become a mother; that was inevitable. This girl who couldn’t even look him in the eyes while standing in front of him would be the mother of his children. Sooner or later.
