“Kill Christopher Davenport,” she read.



Across the county, in his room lit poorly by a lamp still burning, Christopher could not sleep. He got up from his bed and went to the papers spread on the table, full of calculations and arrows. It would still take him a month, perhaps two, to carry out his plan.
