Horizontal lines showed on Daniel’s forehead, furrowed deeply in astonishment “There was no need to tell him anything, Anna. Your husband already knew about our . . .” He paused, searching for the right word, the right epitaph. “What shall we call it? . . . Our morning of madness.”
