I apologize for taking the liberty to write to you, but as you can imagine the anxiety after what happened yesterday—because of me—has given me no peace. Anna, I know that this will oﬀend you, but I have decided to go to London to investigate your husband. I will not ask you again how he was able to get you to marry him, but I cannot manage to convince myself that your feelings for him came on as suddenly as you say
—or that, to quote his words, it “blossomed overnight like a wildﬂower.”
